      "id": "claim_c528799c11f043dd9c0bed8e9367d9e4",
      "statement": "uint8ArrayToBase64 builds the binary string in bounded 0x8000 (32k) chunks before base64-encoding, avoiding a RangeError from String.fromCharCode when the byte count exceeds the engine call-argument limit (~126k on Node v26); base64encode/base64decode use btoa/atob when available and fall back to Node Buffer.",
      "evidence": [
