      "statement": "FingerprintToBase64.encode requires every colon-separated hex token to match /^[0-9A-Fa-f]{1,2}$/ and throws an indexed error on malformed tokens (rejecting silent parseInt coercion of NaN/out-of-range values); decode treats '=' as valid only as the final one-or-two padding characters and rejects any character outside the base64 charset, both throwing on empty/missing input.",
